note irequiv fixture (issue 826): a 32-bit domain, beyond the exhaustive limit.
note pop32 and pop32s (SWAR) can only be compared by sampling, which is not a proof;
note pop32t is a mutant that drops the top bit. spin never returns within the
note interpreter's fuel (16777216 instructions), so its result is INCONCLUSIVE.
note spin runs 1000000 x 20 = 20000000 iterations as two loops: IR mode refuses a
note for count above 1000000 (error 8), the C oracle's range (#857).
fn pop32 x uint to uint
c = uint 0
for i uint 32
c = add c and x 1
x = shr x 1
end
ret c
end
fn pop32s x uint to uint
x = sub x and shr x 1 1431655765
x = add and x 858993459 and shr x 2 858993459
x = and add x shr x 4 252645135
ret shr mul x 16843009 24
end
fn pop32t x uint to uint
x = and x 2147483647
x = sub x and shr x 1 1431655765
x = add and x 858993459 and shr x 2 858993459
x = and add x shr x 4 252645135
ret shr mul x 16843009 24
end
fn spin x uchar to uchar
y = x
for i uint 1000000
for j uint 20
y = add y 1
end
end
ret y
end
